<div class="task-intro gh-intro"><div><p>Most everyday work can start from the Hub’s templates and guides.</p><p>For anything else, from a quick question to a larger project such as new design, video or animation, print, events or business cards, contact the Comms helpdesk. Say what you need, who it’s for and when you need it, and attach anything you already have.</p></div><a href="https://jira.skatelescope.org/servicedesk/customer/portal/364" class="button">Open the Comms helpdesk <span class="arr arr-out" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div><nav class="gh-more" aria-label="More help"><a class="dir-row" href="$link.page('CRH', 'FAQ')"><span class="dir-text"><strong>Common questions</strong><span>Where things are, who approves work, and what to do if something is missing.</span></span></a><a class="dir-row" href="$link.page('CRH', 'How To Submit Your Deck')"><span class="dir-text"><strong>Share material</strong><span>Send a deck, photos, video or a correction for review.</span></span></a></nav>
#elseif($page.id.toString() == "381891657")
<div class="task-intro"><div><span class="eyebrow">Help</span><p>Short answers to the questions staff ask most.</p></div></div><details class="guidance-detail"><summary>Where are templates and slides?</summary><div><p>Start with <a href="$link.page('CRH', 'Templates & Assets')">All resources</a>. Presentation decks are under <a href="$link.page('CRH', 'Slide Decks & Presentations')">Presentations</a>.</p></div></details><details class="guidance-detail"><summary>Where are photos and video?</summary><div><p>In the staff media library in Canto. <a href="$link.page('CRH', 'Photography Media')">Photos and video</a> shows a selection and links to it. Check each asset’s credit and permitted use.</p></div></details><details class="guidance-detail"><summary>Can I adapt material myself?</summary><div><p>Yes, within its usage notes, and keep the credits. Ask the content owner before changing facts or meaning, and the creative team before substantial design changes.</p></div></details><details class="guidance-detail"><summary>Why can I browse but not upload?</summary><div><p>Browsing and contributing have separate permissions. To add material, see <a href="$link.page('CRH', 'How To Submit Your Deck')">Share material</a>.</p></div></details><details class="guidance-detail"><summary>Is my request booked once I send it?</summary><div><p>Not yet. The team replies to agree what will be made and when; a date isn’t fixed until then. If it’s urgent, say why and what could be cut back.</p></div></details><details class="guidance-detail"><summary>Who approves the work?</summary><div><p>Name the content owner and the final reviewer in your request. The approval route depends on the work, so confirm it rather than assume it.</p></div></details><details class="guidance-detail"><summary>A file is missing or a link is broken</summary><div><p>Send the page link and what happened to the <a href="https://jira.skatelescope.org/servicedesk/customer/portal/364">Comms helpdesk <span class="arr arr-out" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>.</p></div></details>
#elseif($page.id.toString() == "381891673")
<div class="task-intro"><div><span class="eyebrow">Do it with confidence</span><p>Practical guidance for work you can do yourself with the Hub’s templates and resources.</p></div></div><div class="directory"><section class="dir-group"><h2>Print and posters</h2><ul class="dir-list"><li><a class="dir-row" href="$link.page('CRH', 'Making Your Own Poster')" data-page-id="381891681"><span class="dir-text"><strong>Prepare a poster</strong><span>Most of the work on a poster happens before you open a template: knowing the size you need and the one thing you want people to remember.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="dir-row" href="$link.page('CRH', 'Preparing Files for Print')" data-page-id="381891685"><span class="dir-text"><strong>Prepare files for print</strong><span>Every supplier and product is a little different, so set up and export your file to the supplier’s specification rather than a one-size-fits-all setting.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="dir-row" href="$link.page('CRH', 'Print Supplier Contacts')" data-page-id="381891885"><span class="dir-text"><strong>Work with print suppliers</strong><span>Communications can recommend trusted print suppliers for your location and the kind of job you have.</span></span></a></li></ul></section><section class="dir-group"><h2>Good practice</h2><ul class="dir-list"><li><a class="dir-row" href="$link.page('CRH', 'Accessibility Guidelines')" data-page-id="381891873"><span class="dir-text"><strong>Accessibility checks</strong><span>Accessible work is easier for everyone to read. Build it in as you go, then check the file you actually share.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="dir-row" href="$link.page('CRH', 'Adobe Firefly')" data-page-id="381891876"><span class="dir-text"><strong>Using AI image tools</strong><span>Use the current SKAO AI policy and approved tools before starting a task.</span></span></a></li></ul></section></div>
#elseif($page.id.toString() == "381891678")
<div class="task-intro"><div><span class="eyebrow">Self-service guide</span><p>A good deck starts from the right template and is built around what your audience needs to take away.</p></div><a href="$link.page('CRH', 'Slide Decks & Presentations')" class="button">Find presentation resources</a></div><ol class="guide-steps"><li><h3>Start from the right template</h3><p>Use the <a href="$link.page('CRH', 'Standard SKAO Template')" class="">Standard SKAO template</a>, or a <a href="$link.page('CRH', 'Partner templates')" class="">partner template</a> for joint work, so the layouts, colours and type are already set.</p></li><li><h3>Give each slide one job</h3><p>Write a short heading that says the point of the slide, and use the supplied layouts so spacing and alignment stay consistent.</p></li><li><h3>Let images and charts explain</h3><p>Use them to make the point rather than decorate, and keep their sources and credits on the slide or in the notes.</p></li><li><h3>Check facts and figures</h3><p>Construction moves quickly, so check facts, dates and any adapted claims with the content owner. The <a href="$link.page('CRH', 'SKA-Low Overview')" class="">SKA-Low</a> and <a href="$link.page('CRH', 'SKA-Mid Overview')" class="">SKA-Mid</a> progress pages have the latest status.</p></li><li><h3>Test it where you’ll present</h3><p>Run the deck on the screen you’ll use and check text and charts read from the back of the room. Check contrast and alternative text, and caption any video.</p></li></ol><nav class="section-next" aria-label="More in Presentations"><div class="section-next-head"><h2>More in Presentations</h2><a class="related-all" href="$link.page('CRH', 'Slide Decks & Presentations')">Prepare a presentation <span class="arr" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div><div class="related-grid"><a class="related-card" href="$link.page('CRH', 'Standard SKAO Template')"><strong>Standard SKAO template</strong><span>A starting layout for a presentation using your own content.</span></a><a class="related-card" href="$link.page('CRH', 'Partner templates')"><strong>Partner templates</strong><span>Presentation templates for joint work with SKAO partners.</span></a><a class="related-card" href="$link.page('CRH', 'About SKAO Master Deck')"><strong>Decks to reuse</strong><span>Approved decks to reuse and adapt: an introduction to the SKAO, the science case, construction progress across both sites, and decks on specialised topics.</span></a></div></nav>
#elseif($page.id.toString() == "381891681")
<div class="task-intro"><div><span class="eyebrow">Self-service guide</span><p>Most of the work on a poster happens before you open a template: knowing the size you need and the one thing you want people to remember.</p></div><a href="$link.page('CRH', 'Poster Templates')" class="button">Check poster templates</a></div><ol class="guide-steps"><li><h3>Check what the organiser needs</h3><p>Find the size, orientation and file format in the call for posters or the organiser’s guidelines. Sizes vary between conferences, so check rather than assume.</p></li><li><h3>Start from an SKAO poster template</h3><p>The <a href="$link.page('CRH', 'Poster Templates')" class="">poster templates</a> come in A0, A1 and A2, with the logo, colours and text styles already set. Pick the one that matches the organiser’s size.</p></li><li><h3>Lead with one clear message</h3><p>Decide the main point first and let the title say it. Add the authors and affiliations, and keep the text short enough to read from a step or two away.</p></li><li><h3>Make it easy to follow</h3><p>Use clear headings and a reading order that runs naturally down the page. Give figures room to breathe, and keep the credit and source with every image and chart.</p></li><li><h3>Export and proof at full size</h3><p>Export a PDF and check it at 100% zoom: images should still look sharp at the printed size. Read it through once more for names, figures and spelling.</p></li></ol><aside class="next-step"><div><h2>Sending it to a printer?</h2><p>Bleed, colour and file settings depend on the supplier.</p></div><a href="$link.page('CRH', 'Preparing Files for Print')" class="text-link">Prepare files for print</a></aside><nav class="section-next" aria-label="More in How-to guides"><div class="section-next-head"><h2>More in How-to guides</h2><a class="related-all" href="$link.page('CRH', 'Self-Service Guides')">Self-service guides <span class="arr" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div><div class="related-grid"><a class="related-card" href="$link.page('CRH', 'Preparing Files for Print')"><strong>Prepare files for print</strong><span>Every supplier and product is a little different, so set up and export your file to the supplier’s specification rather than a one-size-fits-all setting.</span></a><a class="related-card" href="$link.page('CRH', 'Print Supplier Contacts')"><strong>Work with print suppliers</strong><span>Communications can recommend trusted print suppliers for your location and the kind of job you have.</span></a><a class="related-card" href="$link.page('CRH', 'Accessibility Guidelines')"><strong>Accessibility checks</strong><span>Accessible work is easier for everyone to read. Build it in as you go, then check the file you actually share.</span></a></div></nav>
#elseif($page.id.toString() == "381891685")
<div class="task-intro"><div><span class="eyebrow">Before supplier handoff</span><p>Every supplier and product is a little different, so set up and export your file to the supplier’s specification rather than a one-size-fits-all setting.</p></div></div><ol class="guide-steps"><li><h3>Get the supplier’s specification first</h3><p>Ask for the finished size, the bleed and safe area, the colour profile and the PDF standard they accept. If anything is missing from the quote, ask before you export.</p></li><li><h3>Set up bleed and safe area</h3><p>Extend backgrounds and images past the trim by the bleed the supplier asks for, and keep text and logos inside the safe area so nothing important is trimmed off.</p></li><li><h3>Check colour and images</h3><p>Use the colour profile the supplier gives you and make sure images are sharp at the printed size. Spot colours, foils and other special finishes need setting up exactly as the supplier describes.</p></li><li><h3>Export and check the PDF</h3><p>Export to the supplier’s PDF standard with fonts embedded. Then check the PDF itself, not just your design file: text, page order, size and image quality.</p></li><li><h3>Get sign-off before it goes</h3><p>Make sure the content owner has approved the final artwork, and agree the proof, quantity, deadline and delivery details with the supplier.</p></li></ol><aside class="next-step"><div><h2>Not sure about a setting?</h2><p>Send the supplier’s specification and your draft to the Comms helpdesk.</p></div><a href="https://jira.skatelescope.org/servicedesk/customer/portal/364" class="text-link">Ask the Comms helpdesk <span class="arr arr-out" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></aside><nav class="section-next" aria-label="More in How-to guides"><div class="section-next-head"><h2>More in How-to guides</h2><a class="related-all" href="$link.page('CRH', 'Self-Service Guides')">Self-service guides <span class="arr" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div><div class="related-grid"><a class="related-card" href="$link.page('CRH', 'Print Supplier Contacts')"><strong>Work with print suppliers</strong><span>Communications can recommend trusted print suppliers for your location and the kind of job you have.</span></a><a class="related-card" href="$link.page('CRH', 'Accessibility Guidelines')"><strong>Accessibility checks</strong><span>Accessible work is easier for everyone to read. Build it in as you go, then check the file you actually share.</span></a><a class="related-card" href="$link.page('CRH', 'Adobe Firefly')"><strong>Using AI image tools</strong><span>Use the current SKAO AI policy and approved tools before starting a task.</span></a></div></nav>
