<div class="task-intro"><div><span class="eyebrow">Brand essentials</span><p>Use official artwork, preserve its proportions and give it space.</p></div><a href="$link.page('CRH', 'Logos & Icons')" class="button">Find logo files</a></div><section class="reading-section"><h2>Before placing the logo</h2><ul><li>Choose a supplied variant suited to the background.</li><li>Leave at least half the logo’s height clear on all sides (the exclusion zone).</li><li>Do not stretch, recolour, redraw or add effects to the artwork.</li><li>Minimum size: 20 mm wide in print, 50 px wide on screen.</li><li>If the full-colour logo won’t work on your background, use the single-colour logo, usually white on a dark background.</li></ul></section><aside class="next-step"><div><h2>Partner branding?</h2><p>Check the applicable partner guidance before combining identities.</p></div><a href="$link.page('CRH', 'Brand Guidelines')" class="text-link">Return to brand guidance</a></aside><nav class="section-next" aria-label="More in Brand"><div class="section-next-head"><h2>More in Brand</h2><a class="related-all" href="$link.page('CRH', 'Brand Guidelines')">Brand guidance <span class="arr" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div><div class="related-grid"><a class="related-card" href="$link.page('CRH', 'Colour Palette and Typography')"><strong>Colours and typography</strong><span>Official values from the SKAO Brand Book (March 2022). Copy what you need: hex or RGB for screen, CMYK or Pantone for print.</span></a><a class="related-card" href="$link.page('CRH', 'Brand in Practice')"><strong>Apply the brand</strong><span>Use the existing templates and artwork to keep your work recognisably SKAO.</span></a><a class="related-card" href="$link.page('CRH', 'Co-Branding CSIRO')"><strong>Co-branding with CSIRO</strong><span>Guidance for material that carries both the SKAO and CSIRO identities.</span></a></div></nav>
