<div class="task-intro"><div><span class="eyebrow">Make the work usable</span><p>Accessible work is easier for everyone to read. Build it in as you go, then check the file you actually share.</p></div></div><ol class="guide-steps"><li><h3>Use real headings and clear links</h3><p>Use the template’s heading styles rather than bold text, and write links that say where they go. Screen readers rely on both to find their way around.</p></li><li><h3>Describe images that carry meaning</h3><p>Give informative images alternative text that explains what they show and why they’re there. Purely decorative images should be marked as decorative so they’re skipped.</p></li><li><h3>Caption video and transcribe audio</h3><p>Add captions to video and offer a text version of any audio, so the content works with the sound off.</p></li><li><h3>Make text easy to read</h3><p>Check contrast: WCAG’s minimum is generally 4.5:1 for normal text and 3:1 for large text. Don’t rely on colour alone; add labels, symbols or patterns too.</p></li><li><h3>Check the file you share</h3><p>Accessibility can be lost on export, so check the PDF or published version too: reading order, alternative text, and keyboard access and visible focus for anything interactive.</p></li></ol><aside class="next-step"><div><h2>Check the relevant standard</h2><p>These checks are a starting point, not a claim that the work passes a full accessibility audit.</p></div><a href="https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG22/quickref/" class="text-link">Open the W3C reference <span class="arr arr-out" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></aside><nav class="section-next" aria-label="More in How-to guides"><div class="section-next-head"><h2>More in How-to guides</h2><a class="related-all" href="$link.page('CRH', 'Self-Service Guides')">Self-service guides <span class="arr" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div><div class="related-grid"><a class="related-card" href="$link.page('CRH', 'Adobe Firefly')"><strong>Using AI image tools</strong><span>Use the current SKAO AI policy and approved tools before starting a task.</span></a><a class="related-card" href="$link.page('CRH', 'Making Your Own Poster')"><strong>Prepare a poster</strong><span>Most of the work on a poster happens before you open a template: knowing the size you need and the one thing you want people to remember.</span></a><a class="related-card" href="$link.page('CRH', 'Preparing Files for Print')"><strong>Prepare files for print</strong><span>Every supplier and product is a little different, so set up and export your file to the supplier’s specification rather than a one-size-fits-all setting.</span></a></div></nav>
#elseif($page.id.toString() == "381891876")
<div class="task-intro"><div><span class="eyebrow">Concept development</span><p>Use the current SKAO AI policy and approved tools before starting a task.</p></div></div><ol class="guide-steps"><li><h3>Check the material is suitable</h3><p>Only use material the approved service is cleared for, and only data the SKAO AI policy allows. Never upload confidential or personal material.</p></li><li><h3>Use it for concepts</h3><p>AI imagery is good for exploring ideas. Keep it clearly separate from photography and from verified scientific images, so nobody mistakes one for the other.</p></li><li><h3>Check before it goes into a deliverable</h3><p>Verify accuracy, rights and suitability before generated imagery is used in finished work.</p></li></ol><aside class="next-step"><div><h2>Need advice on a creative use?</h2><p>Describe the purpose and proposed output without sending unsuitable source material.</p></div><a href="https://jira.skatelescope.org/servicedesk/customer/portal/364" class="text-link">Ask the creative team <span class="arr arr-out" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></aside><p class="quiet-note">Tool availability, model versions and credit allocations are not confirmed by this page. Check the current approved service and account.</p><nav class="section-next" aria-label="More in How-to guides"><div class="section-next-head"><h2>More in How-to guides</h2><a class="related-all" href="$link.page('CRH', 'Self-Service Guides')">Self-service guides <span class="arr" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div><div class="related-grid"><a class="related-card" href="$link.page('CRH', 'Making Your Own Poster')"><strong>Prepare a poster</strong><span>Most of the work on a poster happens before you open a template: knowing the size you need and the one thing you want people to remember.</span></a><a class="related-card" href="$link.page('CRH', 'Preparing Files for Print')"><strong>Prepare files for print</strong><span>Every supplier and product is a little different, so set up and export your file to the supplier’s specification rather than a one-size-fits-all setting.</span></a><a class="related-card" href="$link.page('CRH', 'Print Supplier Contacts')"><strong>Work with print suppliers</strong><span>Communications can recommend trusted print suppliers for your location and the kind of job you have.</span></a></div></nav>
