<div class="task-intro"><div><span class="eyebrow">Typography</span><p>Use Noto Sans for the SKAO identity, with Verdana as the fallback.</p></div><a href="https://fonts.google.com/noto/specimen/Noto+Sans" class="button">Open Noto Sans at Google Fonts <span class="arr arr-out" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div><section class="reading-section"><h2>Which weight to use</h2><ul><li><strong>Noto Sans Light</strong>: headlines, body text and long paragraphs.</li><li><strong>Noto Sans Medium</strong>: emphasis within body copy and bold headlines.</li><li><strong>Noto Sans Regular and Bold</strong>: small type, text over backgrounds, or where Light becomes hard to read.</li><li><strong>Noto Mono</strong>: technical text, metrics and footnotes, used sparingly.</li><li><strong>Verdana</strong>: the fallback when Noto Sans is not available.</li></ul></section><section class="reading-section"><h2>Use in your work</h2><ul><li>Follow the template’s existing text styles where available.</li><li>Use your organisation’s approved installation route on a managed device.</li><li>Check the font in the exported or shared file, particularly when moving between applications.</li></ul></section><aside class="next-step"><div><h2>Can’t install the font?</h2><p>Use the fallback and ask for help through your usual IT support route.</p></div><a href="$link.page('CRH', 'Colour Palette and Typography')" class="text-link">Return to typography guidance</a></aside><nav class="section-next" aria-label="More in Brand"><div class="section-next-head"><h2>More in Brand</h2><a class="related-all" href="$link.page('CRH', 'Brand Guidelines')">Brand guidance <span class="arr" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div><div class="related-grid"><a class="related-card" href="$link.page('CRH', 'SKAO Brand Book')"><strong>SKAO Brand Book</strong><span>The Brand Book is the detailed source for visual identity rules.</span></a><a class="related-card" href="$link.page('CRH', 'Logo Usage and Downloads')"><strong>Using the SKAO logo</strong><span>Use official artwork, preserve its proportions and give it space.</span></a><a class="related-card" href="$link.page('CRH', 'Colour Palette and Typography')"><strong>Colours and typography</strong><span>Official values from the SKAO Brand Book (March 2022). Copy what you need: hex or RGB for screen, CMYK or Pantone for print.</span></a></div></nav>
#elseif($page.id.toString() == "381891885")
<div class="task-intro"><div><span class="eyebrow">Production handoff</span><p>Communications can recommend trusted print suppliers for your location and the kind of job you have.</p></div><a href="https://jira.skatelescope.org/servicedesk/customer/portal/364" class="button">Ask for a supplier recommendation <span class="arr arr-out" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div><ol class="guide-steps"><li><h3>Ask us for a recommendation</h3><p>Tell us where you are and where the items need to go, what you need printed, its size and quantity, and your deadline and budget. We’ll suggest suppliers that suit the job.</p></li><li><h3>Follow the purchasing process</h3><p>Check which procurement rules apply with the responsible team, and agree who gets the quote, who approves the spend and who places the order.</p></li><li><h3>Agree sign-off and dates</h3><p>Decide who signs off the content and the final proof, and agree production and delivery dates with the supplier before you commit.</p></li><li><h3>Prepare the files</h3><p>Ask the supplier for their specification and set up your artwork to match. <a href="$link.page('CRH', 'Preparing Files for Print')" class="">Prepare files for print</a> walks through it.</p></li></ol><nav class="section-next" aria-label="More in How-to guides"><div class="section-next-head"><h2>More in How-to guides</h2><a class="related-all" href="$link.page('CRH', 'Self-Service Guides')">Self-service guides <span class="arr" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div><div class="related-grid"><a class="related-card" href="$link.page('CRH', 'Accessibility Guidelines')"><strong>Accessibility checks</strong><span>Accessible work is easier for everyone to read. Build it in as you go, then check the file you actually share.</span></a><a class="related-card" href="$link.page('CRH', 'Adobe Firefly')"><strong>Using AI image tools</strong><span>Use the current SKAO AI policy and approved tools before starting a task.</span></a><a class="related-card" href="$link.page('CRH', 'Making Your Own Poster')"><strong>Prepare a poster</strong><span>Most of the work on a poster happens before you open a template: knowing the size you need and the one thing you want people to remember.</span></a></div></nav>
